[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit"]
[Variation "Slav Defence, Czech Variation"]
[ECO "D17"]
[Character "positional,solid"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "a4-bind,bishop-trade"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 c6 { The Slav: Black guards d5 with a pawn so the c8 bishop can still come out. }
3. Nf3 { Develops and watches e5 and d4. } 3... Nf6
4. Nc3 { Adds a second guard of the centre and a second attacker on d5. } 4... dxc4 ( 4... e6 5. e3 { A solid choice against the Semi-Slav: White develops and keeps the centre, then waits to see how Black plays. } 5... Nbd7 6. Bd3 dxc4 7. Bxc4 b5 8. Bd3 a6 9. e4 )
5. a4 { Stops ...b5, which would let Black keep the extra pawn on c4. [%csl Gb5] } 5... Bf5
6. e3 { Opens the bishop on f1 so it can take back on c4. } 6... e6 ( 6... a6 7. Ne5 { Claims the centre and eyes c4 and f7. } )
7. Bxc4 Bb4 { Pins the knight on c3 against the king. } 8. O-O Nbd7
9. Qe2 { Prepares e4 and defends the bishop on c4. } 9... Bg6
10. e4 { Takes the centre at last, with a lead in development. } 10... O-O 11. Bd3 { Moves the bishop to a safer square, where it still supports e4 and eyes Black's king side. } *
